<?php

namespace App\Services;

class AskLucidKnowledge
{
    public function text(): string
    {
        $mb = (int) config('supportflow.workspaces.max_file_bytes') / 1024 / 1024;
        $batch = (int) config('supportflow.workspaces.max_batch');
        $files = (int) config('supportflow.workspaces.max_documents');
        $characters = number_format((int) config('supportflow.workspaces.max_extracted_characters'));
        $days = (int) config('supportflow.workspaces.lifetime_days');
        $invoiceMb = (int) config('supportflow.invoices.max_file_bytes') / 1024 / 1024;
        $invoiceDays = (int) config('supportflow.invoices.lifetime_days');

        return <<<TEXT
Lucid: 'Custom software. Practical AI.' A working portfolio/showroom for customizable business workflows: Customer support, Document chat and Invoice review. Explore demos on Home opens three demo cards. Visitors explore without signup. The demo offers no paid subscription, production accounting integration, real refunds/shipping/email or live human support. Demo Agent desk access is public demo access, not private production staff access. Use fictional details and non-sensitive files. Privacy explains data practices.
Ask Lucid explains the app; it cannot read screens, files, tickets, internal notes, or other chats. Coarse page/layout hints only orient it. Questions, recent Ask Lucid history and approved product knowledge go to OpenAI. Ask Lucid history is browser-session scoped in application cache for 45 minutes after the last answer, keeping up to 12 question/answer pairs. Closing/minimizing preserves it; refresh/navigation restores it within that session. New chat clears only Ask Lucid history, not Harbor chat/documents/settings/tickets/invoices. Stop keeps your question and the text already shown, marked Stopped. Failed partial answers are not retained. No live-agent transfer for Lucid product help.
Shared layout: left navigation opens demos, Agent desk and Browse policies. Hide instructions/Show instructions control guidance visibility; collapsing navigation is visual only. Guidance changes with task stage/tabs/results. A separate instruction column becomes guidance below the workspace on stacked layouts. Describe only the layout supplied. Sources identify supporting passages; AI answers still need review.
Customer support is a fictional Harbor Outfitters retail demo. Customer chat answers from published Harbor policies with numbered references. Follow-ups retain context. References open Sources & actions; Open policy opens that public article; Browse policies opens the full catalog. Restart demo confirms clearing Harbor chat, returns and replacement requests, then returns to the beginning. Submitted tickets stay available in Agent desk. It is separate from Ask Lucid New chat. Return proposals need explicit confirmation; Cancel saves no proposed action. The 79-dollar Trail Pack demonstrates a low-value return; the 249-dollar tent demonstrates staff review. Confirmation shows a saved reference; no actual refund or shipping label is issued. Create a support ticket submits a Harbor request to demo Agent desk. Customer receipt/link shows public updates and an approved sent reply, never private notes or unsent drafts. Anyone with that private link can read public updates; don't share it publicly. This retail ticket flow isn't a Lucid product-support channel. Undocumented policy must not become invented promises.
Agent desk Dashboard summarizes current demo records/counts/charts, not business performance guarantees. Tickets queue supports status/source filters and pagination, with no text-search control and opens Ticket review. Scenario cards demonstrate varied support cases. AI intake summarizes/classifies, estimates priority/sentiment/confidence, and may draft a policy-grounded reply. Confidence is an assessment, not a guaranteed probability. AI reviewing means processing; Awaiting review means a draft needs human approval; Escalated means human attention, not sent; AI unavailable means failure with Retry AI. Angry cases escalate without a draft. No reply sends automatically.
Ticket review: Review reply holds suggested/manual replies. Save edits saves without sending; Approve and send publishes the approved reply to the demo customer's receipt. Reject discards a suggestion; Regenerate requests new wording with the same grounded facts, or keeps the matching draft with notice. Manual reply lets a person write their own text. Reply history contains approved public messages. Sources show supporting policies. Details edits classifications/status independently of sending; Activity shows workflow events. Internal notes are team-only and never customer-visible. Notes/history/activity expand older entries inline, then return to recent. Copy customer link copies the receipt URL. Clear inactive demo data removes eligible stale demo data, not every active record; don't advise deletion casually.
Document chat is upload-only: your own readable PDF, DOCX, TXT or Markdown (.md), no sample-loading shortcut. Limits: $mb MB per file, $batch files per upload, $files documents per workspace, $characters extracted characters per file. Combined batch allowances don't raise per-file limits. Documents belong to a private workspace, separate from public Harbor policies. Reading/processing means preparing text; Ready for answers means available; Failed means unavailable. Ready files remain usable alongside failed files. Blank/whitespace needs text. No readable text in a PDF/DOCX may mean blank or image-only; no OCR/photo extraction. Protected/corrupt/unsupported/oversized files require a supported readable replacement. File acceptance doesn't guarantee complete answers.
Ask Document chat for summaries, deadlines, comparisons or applications of documented rules; name a file/topic when multiple are uploaded. Ambiguous singular summaries can require clarification. Large overviews can sample passages and disclose incomplete coverage. Calculations need documented inputs. Answers use available passages, not the internet. Numbered sources open exact private passages, in a right source panel with separate columns or a source dialog in stacked layout. Back to instructions/close restores guidance. No invented public links/page numbers.
Answer settings: Professional/Friendly/Matter-of-fact tone; Concise/Standard/Thorough length; Add instruction for preferences, then Save settings. Preferences change wording, never facts. Settings survive New chat/refresh. New chat confirms clearing conversation only, retaining files/settings. Add documents adds files; Remove deletes one file. Start fresh confirms permanent deletion of files, conversation and saved settings, invalidating its return code. Privacy & access shows expiry/return code; keep the code private. Open a previous workspace reopens using that code. Hiding the code doesn't save/discard it. Workspaces expire after $days days; deleted/expired access cannot recover files. Ask Lucid cannot obtain codes or summarize uploads: use Document chat.
Invoice review accepts one text-readable supplier invoice PDF at a time up to $invoiceMb MB; no scans/photos/OCR. Try a sample invoice uses the same extraction/review pipeline as uploads. Choose file then Extract fields uploads your own PDF. Processing proposes editable supplier, invoice number/date, currency, tax, invoice total and line items. A line item is one product/service row: description, quantity, unit price, line total. Compare all fields against the original: matching math doesn't prove correct extraction, supplier authenticity, tax treatment, payment or accounting approval.
Amounts don't match means a quantity times unit price differs from its line total, or line totals plus tax differ from invoice total. Warnings name each affected field/row and show entered/calculated amounts. Go to links focus the field; visible fields stay in place, off-screen fields scroll with label visible. Check the PDF, correct values, Save corrections below Line items, repeat remaining issues. Confirm invoice is blocked until required values are valid and amounts match; confirmation is explicit. Confirmed fields are read-only. Download CSV is for spreadsheets with decimal amounts and currency column; Download JSON is for custom software/automation with integer cents (22745 means 227.45). Exports don't pay/post/sync accounting records. No fixed documented line-item cap; acceptance doesn't guarantee unlimited row extraction. A 24-line two-page invoice was verified, not every format.
Northwind built-in fictional sample has four rows and three intentional discrepancies: Line 1 62.80 becomes 59.70; Line 4 34.80 becomes 36.80; Invoice total 237.45 becomes 227.45. Correct line totals sum to 210.60, plus tax 16.85 = 227.45. Those corrections apply only to that sample, not arbitrary uploads.
View original PDF opens an in-tab floating panel in the separate-column layout. Drag to move, Resize preview, Close preview and Open PDF in new tab control it. Keep editing visible fields while open. Native PDF annotation tools belong to the browser and don't overwrite Lucid's original/fields. Stacked layout uses Show original PDF / Show invoice fields, preserving unsaved edits. Private originals check owning browser/expiry. Back to invoice choices at the top clears current selection/unsaved edits and returns to sample/upload choices; stored invoices/PDFs remain until normal $invoiceDays-day expiry/cleanup. Download needed results before leaving. Failed extraction cannot be confirmed; follow its error/retry guidance.
Privacy/safety: OpenAI processes relevant questions/passages/invoice text/transcription audio. Lucid has not opted into training data sharing; provider retention is separate from Lucid cleanup. Don't promise zero retention or compliance certifications. Document workspaces/invoices expire automatically; Start fresh can delete a workspace sooner. Internal notes and unsent drafts aren't public receipts. Microphone requests browser permission and transcribes into the editor; recording alone never sends. In Customer chat, Document chat and Ask Lucid, explicit Send stops recording, waits for final transcription and sends once; Stop dictation only finalizes an editable draft. Failed or empty transcription keeps the draft without sending. Recording stays with its original draft while browsing Lucid or switching app focus, subject to browser/device support, limits and failures. Browser support varies and physical-device acceptance remains separate. Ask Lucid uses the shared microphone control. Stop answer stops generation, not document processing or an invoice job.
TEXT;
    }
